Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "How to use this notebook:\n\t1. Run the whole section \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Preliminaries\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] once from top to \
bottom. This loads the packages, sets the notebook directory, imports the \
\[Chi] tables and EOS GG parameter files, and defines the helper functions \
used everywhere else.\n\t2. After the setup finishes, move to the section \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Calculations\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and evaluate only \
the commands relevant to the task at hand. This section presents several \
examples illustrating how to use the code.\n\t3. To generate posterior \
samples for one process, use the cells in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Samples\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], e.g. \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["GGProcessSamples[GGparams[\"bc\"],\"BD\",n]", "Code"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\t4. To produce figures, use the cells in \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Plots\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], e.g. \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["PlotEOSGGfit[\"BD\", \"f+\", n]", "Code"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\t5. Keep the notebook in its current folder \
structure: several setup cells load files through relative paths such as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]chi/\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]GG_parameters/\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.818240196147729*^9, 3.818240197378016*^9}, 
